CS612 Assignment 3: Cache Lab

Read ASSIGNMENT.pdf first. It has the full specification, the grading
scheme, and the report you must submit.

You modify and submit two files:
  csim.c        Part A: your cache simulator
  trans.c       Part B: your cache-friendly transpose

Build everything (requires gcc, make, python3, valgrind):
  linux> make

Check Part A (your simulator against the reference simulator):
  linux> ./test-csim

Check Part B (correctness and misses of every registered transpose):
  linux> ./test-trans -M 48 -N 48
  linux> ./test-trans -M 48 -N 64
  linux> ./test-trans -M 59 -N 73

Check everything at once (this is the same program the course staff (Madhav or I) use to grade your work):
  linux> ./driver.py

See which accesses of transpose function i hit and miss:
  linux> ./csim-ref -v -s 5 -E 1 -b 5 -t trace.f<i>

Prepare your submission (three files, prefixed with your roll number):
  linux> make submit ROLL=<your roll number>

Other files (do not modify):
  Makefile        Builds the simulator and the tools
  cachelab.c/.h   Helper functions, including printSummary()
  bin/            Reference simulator binaries (x86-64 and ARM64);
                  make copies the right one to ./csim-ref
  test-csim.c     Compares csim with csim-ref on the graded test cases
  test-trans.c    Measures the misses of your transpose functions
  tracegen.c      Helper used by test-trans
  driver.py       Runs all tests and prints your autograded score
  traces/         Trace files used by test-csim
